@startuml sequence_hook_context
!include ../../../design/theme.iuml

mainframe **sd** Hook Context Namespacing & Flow

participant "Pipeline" as Eval
participant "Hook Executor" as Exec
participant "Auth Plugin\n(critical, pri=1)" as Auth
participant "RateLimiter Plugin\n(critical, pri=2)" as RL
participant "Audit Plugin\n(non-critical post hook)" as Audit

== Context Initialization ==

Eval -> Eval : ctx = command.NewHookCtx()
Eval -> Eval : op = tracker.Start(TypeCommand)\nctx["_operation_id"] = op.ID\nctx["_start_ns"] = now()
note right : ctx = {\n  _operation_id: "cmd_42",\n  _start_ns: "171..."\n}

== Operation Hooks (before command hooks) ==

Exec -> Exec : Operation-hook executor may enrich\noperation context synchronously
note right : Example: tracing hook writes\nshared.traceparent before\ncommand hooks see it.

== Pre-Hook: Auth (priority 1) ==

Exec -> Auth : HookRequestV1\ncontext: {_operation_id, _start_ns, shared.*}
Auth --> Exec : HookResponseV1\ncontext_values: {tenant_id: "acme", shared.user: "john"}
Exec -> Exec : command.MergeHookCtx(ctx, "auth", values)

== Pre-Hook: RateLimiter (priority 2) ==

Exec -> RL : HookRequestV1\ncontext: {_operation_id, _start_ns, shared.user}
note right : Filter hides auth.* from RateLimiter.
RL --> Exec : HookResponseV1\ncontext_values: {remaining: "42"}
Exec -> Exec : command.MergeHookCtx(ctx, "ratelimiter", values)

== Command Execution ==

Eval -> Eval : execute command
Eval -> Eval : ctx["_elapsed_ns"] = "150000"

== Post-Hook: Audit (optional reaction point) ==

Exec ->> Audit : HookRequestV1 POST\ncontext: {_operation_id, _start_ns, _elapsed_ns, shared.*}
note right
  Post-hooks are reaction points.
  Prometheus metrics are query-only, and
  runtime instrumentation consumes async events.
end note

@enduml
